sue](https://github.com/nzakas/eslint/issues/158#issuecomment-28396651).\n\n---\n\nThe Rule ID 'no-extra-semi' does _not_ appear to be _on_ by default in eslint v0.1.0 (npm version), node v0.10.21\n\nIn the following code, I get a double `Warning - Unnecessary semicolon.` (as expected) from _jshint_, but not from _eslint_:\n\n```\n/*global console */\n/*eslint no-console:0 */ /*no-extra-semi:1*/\n\n(function() {\n    \"use strict\";\n\n    var x = 3;;\n\n    while(true) {\n        console.log(\"OMG LOOP!\");\n    };\n})();\n```\n\neslint output:\n\n```\n>eslint lint.test.js\nlint.test.js: line 5, col 4, Error - Expected an assignment or function call and instead saw an expression.\nlint.test.js: line 7, col 8, Error - x is defined but never used\n\n2 problems\n```\n\nBoth of the eslint-reported issues are as currently expected.\n\nBut only by changing the eslint directives to  `/*eslint no-console:0 no-extra-semi:1*/` do I get the expected output  `Warning - Unnecessary semicolon.`\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/28542564/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"MichaelPaulukonis","id":2607898,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDc4OTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2607898?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelPaulukonis","html_url":"https://github.com/MichaelPaulukonis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelPaulukonis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelPaulukonis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelPaulukonis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelPaulukonis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelPaulukonis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.githu